{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966781,"nonce":"3uurz8DCyMVI8ZZOkUuh29Uqhq0=","title":"cn Button kept its old width when its label changed. Two unrelated causes - a snapshotted","message":"Symptom: a cn Button's container is one update behind its text. \"Save\" -\u003e\n\"Saving...\" keeps the narrow box and clips; back to \"Save\" keeps the wide box.\n**Two independent causes**, in different code paths. Fixed `a47f41da` and\n`1ec678b1`.\n\n\n`cn::Button::from_config` did `current(\u0026config.label)` and the `on_state`\nclosure captured that `String`, so a refresh re-rendered the build-time text.\nThe topology hash therefore did not change, `refresh_props_internal` took the\nvisual-only branch of its three-tier discrimination, and nothing re-measured.\nFix: read from the reactive source inside the callback; keep the snapshot only\nfor the icon-only decision, which cannot change without a rebuild.\n\nAlso `layout Button::deps()` stored signals but never called\n`register_stateful_deps` -- that happens in `on_state`, from whatever deps are\nset at that moment. cn Button calls `.on_state(...)` then `.deps(...)`, so it\nregistered an empty list and was skipped by the `is_empty` guard. Every other cn\nwidget puts `.deps()` first, so Button was the only one affected. `deps()` now\nregisters too.\n\n\n`Button` holds its state callback until `register_state_callback()` installs it\non the inner `Stateful`. `children_builders()` delegated without installing, so\nit reported a childless box. A parent Stateful's refresh hashes rebuilt content\nthrough `children_builders` to choose structural-vs-visual, so a\n`dropdown_menu_custom` trigger swapping \"Custom Trigger\" (140px) for\n\"Close Menu\" (109px) hashed identically and never re-measured.\n`render_props()` already had this mirror, with a comment naming\n`dropdown_menu_custom` from an earlier round. `children_builders` needed it too.\n\nCause 2 is NOT bound-prop related -- the parent builds a fresh `cn::button`\nwith a plain `\u0026str` each refresh -- which is why the DSL playground was\nunaffected and the cn_demo trigger was not.\n\n\n`crates/blinc_cn/tests/button_label_resize.rs`. Rebuilding a `RenderTree` from\nscratch NEVER reproduces it; these are in-place refresh bugs. The harness needs:\n\n- write through `Signal::set`, not `State::set` -- `State::set` notifies\n  statefuls only via a per-instance callback that `State::new` does not install\n- install the notifier the host does:\n  `set_stateful_deps_notifier(|ids| blinc_layout::check_stateful_deps(ids))`\n- call `tree.process_pending_subtree_rebuilds()` -- a refresh only QUEUES the\n  rebuild\n- test BOTH directions. Grow passed while shrink failed, and a container that\n  only grows looks exactly like \"not resizing\" for a label that starts long.\n\nAlso worth knowing: a hard-coded wrapper width (`div().w(100.0)`) clips any\nlabel that outgrows it and looks identical to this bug. Use `w_fit()`; a bare\n`div()` is `Auto`, not fit-content.\n\nSee gotcha element builder trait forwarding,\nproject cn reactive prop migration.","files":null}]}